# Wiki Rules

This folder is an LLM Wiki. The LLM reads sources in `raw/` and grows the pages in `wiki/`. Humans read it in Obsidian.
The rules in this file take precedence over any CLAUDE.md in parent folders. Edit them freely to fit the project.

## Language

- Write everything in this wiki in English: pages, `index.md`, `log.md`, and `wiki/glossary.md`. Source material saved to `raw/` keeps its original language, but write the header you add to it (source, date, notes) in English.
- Write in English even when the source material or the conversation is in another language. Translate the facts; do not paste untranslated prose.
- Keep code, identifiers, file paths, commands, error messages, and product or proper names exactly as they appear. When a non-English business term matters, write the English term and add the original in parentheses once, e.g. `prescription refill (処方箋の再調剤)`, and add the original to `aliases`.
- Quotes from sources may stay in the original language when the exact wording matters. Add an English translation after them.

## Directories

| Path | Role | How the LLM treats it |
|---|---|---|
| `raw/YYYY/MM/MM-DD-topic-name.md` | Source material (PR summaries, meeting notes, chat excerpts, search results) | Preserve source contents |
| `raw/inbox/` | Pending, unverified automatic candidates | Review before ingestion |
| `wiki/repos/` | Overview of each repository | Create and update |
| `wiki/features/` | One page per feature | Create and update |
| `wiki/decisions/` | Design decisions (why it was done this way) | Create and update |
| `wiki/problems/` | Incidents, gotchas, and their fixes | Create and update |
| `wiki/glossary.md` | Business terms | Append |
| `index.md` | Table of contents for all pages | Update every time |
| `log.md` | Operation history (newest first) | Append every time |

Save sources using their source date, or the ingestion date when unknown, and an English kebab-case title. Example: `raw/2026/10/10-09-logic-pitch-correction.md`. Create year/month directories as needed. Check existing directories and local rules before saving. Reuse an identical source; add a distinguishing identifier for a different source rather than overwriting it.

Move processed inbox candidates into the same dated layout without changing their contents, including rejected candidates. Include a session identifier in candidate titles. Do not save new processed sources in `raw/sessions/`.

When the user requests a layout migration, update all affected links, including links inside raw sources, and verify that no old references or broken links remain. Preserve all other source contents. Do not migrate existing sources merely to ingest a new source.

## Writing pages

- One topic per page. Use English `kebab-case` file names.
- Start each page with frontmatter.

  ```yaml
  ---
  id: <file name>
  aliases: []
  tags: [<project name>, <repo|feature|decision|problem>]
  sources: ["[[raw/YYYY/MM/MM-DD-topic-name]]"]
  updated: YYYY-MM-DD
  verified: YYYY-MM-DD  # optional. Date the code evidence was last checked
  ---
  ```

- Put a 1-3 line summary at the top of the body.
- Link related pages with `[[page name]]`. The target may not exist yet (it becomes a candidate page).
- Cite a source for every fact (a file in `raw/`, a PR number, an Issue number). Mark guesses with "Speculation:".
- For facts learned by reading code, put (evidence: `repo://<project>/<path>#L<a>-L<b>@<sha>`) right after the fact. Create the reference with `llm_wiki.py claim-ref`. Check whether the code behind it changed with `llm_wiki.py check-claims`.
- Do not delete outdated statements. Strike them through with `~~strikethrough~~`, add the date, and write the new statement below.
- Never write secrets (tokens, passwords, personal information).

### decisions template

```markdown
## Context
## Decision
## Alternatives considered
## Consequences and trade-offs
```

### problems template

```markdown
## Symptoms
## Cause
## Fix
## Prevention
```

Follow the llm-wiki plugin skills for the procedures (Ingest / Query / Lint).
